report: "---\nauthor: \"builder\"\ncreated: \"2026-11-23\"\nupdated: \"2026-11-23\"\n---\n\n# Test byteArray ranking under the shim on llm\n\n**Result:** llm is not affected. The ported regression tests pass on llm\nunchanged, so the pull request is tests only, with no changeset (llm's\nCONTRIBUTING.md lists \"Test additions or fixes\" as not needing one).\n\nCommit `d4af0b0e1` sits on branch `test-marshal-bytearray-rank-shim` (and on\nthe job branch `job/marshal-bytearray-rank-shim-llm/1`) in\n`endojs/endo-but-for-bots`, based on `llm` at `036876777`. The commit author\nis the garden placeholder `garden <garden@garden.invalid>`. Re-author it\nbefore pushing if you want a different author.\n\n## Proposed pull request\n\nBase `llm`, head `test-marshal-bytearray-rank-shim`, draft.\n\n**Title:** `test(marshal,patterns): rank equal-length byteArrays under the shim`\n\n**Body:**\n\n> On endojs/endo master, under the `@endo/immutable-arraybuffer` shim, any two\n> byteArrays of the same length rank as tied: `rankOrder.js` reads them through\n> `new Uint8Array(buffer)`, and that is an empty view over the shim's buffer.\n> The upstream fix is in job `marshal-bytearray-rank-shim-fix`.\n>\n> llm is not affected, and this PR adds tests to keep it that way. Since\n> d9b773e06 (#475), a byteArray on llm is a frozen `Uint8Array`, and llm\n> reads its bytes correctly in three independent places:\n>\n> - the llm shim makes `new Uint8Array(immutableBuffer)` a full-length\n>   emulated wrapper, not master's empty view;\n> - `rankOrder.js` copies each byteArray with `slice(0)` before comparing;\n> - `compareBytes` (`@endo/bytes`) copies any emulated wrapper itself through\n>   `toIndexableUint8Array`.\n>\n> The new tests port the upstream regression cases:\n>\n> - `packages/marshal/test/rankOrder.test.js`: equal-length byteArrays of\n>   length 1 and 3, with the first difference at the start, middle and end,\n>   through `compareRank` and `compareAntiRank`. Also equal contents at lengths\n>   0, 1 and 3, shorter-before-longer, and a `sortByRank` of a mixed list.\n> - `packages/patterns/test/byteArray-key-order.test.js` (new):\n>   `compareKeys`, `keyEQ` and `matches`, including a byteArray nested in an\n>   array. patterns had no test that compared byteArray contents.\n>\n> `encodePassable` reads bytes through `thawedBytes` and `encodeHex`, and the\n> existing `byteArray.test.js` and `encodePassable.test.js` already cover it\n> with equal-length cases, so this PR adds nothing there.\n>\n> No changeset, because this PR only adds tests.\n\n## What I ran\n\nNode v22.22.1, which has no native immutable ArrayBuffer, so every run used\nthe shim. The new test logs `emulated immutable ArrayBuffers (shim)`.\n\n- `yarn test` in `packages/marshal`: 97 passed, 1 skipped, under each of the\n  lockdown, unsafe, endo and default configs.\n- `yarn test` in `packages/patterns`: 702 passed under each of the lockdown,\n  unsafe and endo configs.\n- `yarn eslint` on both test files: no errors. The one warning is the\n  `@ts-nocheck` already on line 1 of `rankOrder.test.js`.\n- `yarn prettier --check` on both files: clean.\n- `yarn lint:types` in `packages/patterns`: clean.\n- `garden prose diff llm`: no findings.\n\nI did not run the whole repository's lint or test suite, only the two\npackages I touched.\n\n### Are the tests load-bearing?\n\nI ran temporary mutants and reverted each one:\n\n| Mutant | New tests |\n| --- | --- |\n| A: `rankOrder.js` reads `new Uint8Array(left.buffer)` (the master pattern) | pass, because the llm shim makes that a full wrapper and `compareBytes` copies it |\n| B: `rankOrder.js` drops `slice(0)` | pass, because `compareBytes` copies |\n| C: B, plus `toIndexableUint8Array` returns its input unchanged | **fail** in every config: equal-length byteArrays tie (`compareRank` returns 0), the same symptom as master. Both patterns tests fail too |\n| E: `encodePassable` drops `thawedBytes`, plus C's `toIndexableUint8Array` change | existing `byteArray.test.js` and `encodePassable.test.js` tests fail |\n\nSo the new tests catch the failure only when every defense is gone. Each\ndefense alone keeps llm correct. llm's existing test `compareRank orders\nbyteArrays by shortlex, reading bytes correctly` also fails under mutant C.\nThe new tests add the length-1, middle-difference, equal-contents and sort\ncases, plus the patterns coverage.\n\n## How llm differs from master\n\nOn master, a byteArray is an immutable `ArrayBuffer`, and `new\nUint8Array(buffer)` over the shim's buffer is empty, so every comparison sees\nzero bytes. On llm, `new Uint8Array(buffer)` gives a wrapper of the right\nlength, but that wrapper has no integer-indexed bytes (`wrapper[0]` is\n`undefined`, `ArrayBuffer.isView` is false). A reader that indexed the\nwrapper directly would fail the same way master does (mutant C), but llm has\nno such reader on these paths.\n\n## Environment notes\n\n- `garden project add` failed with git's \"dubious ownership\" error on the\n  shared repository. I added a `safe.directory` entry to the slot's own\n  `~/.gitconfig`.\n- `yarn install` needed `COREPACK_HOME` outside the slot (the shed's\n  `\"type\": \"module\"` made Yarn load as ESM), `TMPDIR` under `scratch/`\n  (`/tmp` is `noexec`), and `--mode=skip-build` (better-sqlite3's native\n  build failed; marshal and patterns do not need it).\n- I recorded these in `roles/PLOT.md` for the next worker.\n- I read the upstream test from branch `job/marshal-bytearray-rank-shim-fix/2`\n  in the garden's `endojs/endo` repository and adapted it to llm's\n  byteArray form, a frozen `Uint8Array` instead of an immutable `ArrayBuffer`.\n"
